Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL HOS] Input: himax-spi: bound coordinates before inversion

Edge compensation can produce raw x=2560 or y=1600 for a panel whose
inclusive maxima are 2559 and 1599. Inverting x before the DT-requested
axis swap then reports ABS_Y=-1. Clamp signed raw coordinates to the
touchscreen properties' inclusive bounds before the existing transform.

Interior positions, contact tracking, pressure, palm detection and rotation
order are unchanged. This corrects edge overflow only; it does not claim
to fix interrupted or insensitive swipes in the screen interior.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
@@ -1076,7 +1076,11 @@
 		if (!on)
 			continue;
 
+		/* Edge compensation may reach size, one past the inclusive max.
+		 * Clamp while signed, before inversion and axis swapping.
+		 */
 		touchscreen_report_pos(ts->input_dev, &ts->props,
-				       ts->algo->tracks[i].x, ts->algo->tracks[i].y, true);
+				       clamp_t(s32, ts->algo->tracks[i].x, 0, ts->props.max_x),
+				       clamp_t(s32, ts->algo->tracks[i].y, 0, ts->props.max_y), true);
 		if (!disable_pressure) {
 			if (ts->algo->pressure_enabled) {
